RB5009 IPv4 ACCESS MAP — CURRENT COMMITTED POLICY
Committed: 2026-08-23

This is an operational note, not an importable RouterOS script.
The live firewall rules remain the authoritative configuration.


WIREGUARD ADMIN IDENTITIES
==========================

HOST-ADMIN contains exactly:

  192.168.90.2/32   Mario's Pixel 9
  192.168.90.3/32   Mario's ThinkPad / Fedora

Both peers receive the same permissions. A new WireGuard peer does not receive
administrative access automatically; its individual tunnel address must first
be added to HOST-ADMIN.


WIREGUARD ENTRY TO THE ROUTER
=============================

WireGuard handshake:

  UDP 13231 is accepted from the WAN interface list.
  UDP 13231 is also accepted from VLAN30 (192.168.30.0/24), allowing a local
  trusted device to establish the tunnel without leaving the LAN.

Once authenticated through wireguard1, a HOST-ADMIN peer may access the RB5009:

  TCP 22       SSH
  TCP 443      HTTPS / the configured TCP 443 service
  TCP 8291     WinBox
  ICMP         Ping and related IPv4 diagnostics

Other WireGuard-to-router IPv4 traffic is denied unless another earlier,
explicit firewall rule permits it.


