VLAN-TO-ROUTER SUMMARY
======================

VLAN10 — OOB/KVM

  Allowed to RB5009: DHCP (UDP 67), DNS (UDP/TCP 53), ICMP.
  Router management is not generally allowed directly from VLAN10.
  Management of VLAN10 devices is available from an authenticated WG admin on
  TCP 22/80/443 and ICMP.

VLAN20 — infrastructure management

  Allowed to RB5009: existing DNS and ICMP rules.
  Infrastructure may access the Internet under the existing explicit rule.
  Initiating connections into other private networks is blocked.
  Router administration should be performed through WireGuard.

VLAN30 — trusted clients

  Allowed to RB5009: DHCP, DNS and ICMP.
  Other direct router access, including SSH/HTTPS/WinBox, is blocked.
  Internet access remains allowed.
  Initiating connections into private networks is blocked except for any
  narrow, pre-existing explicit service rules (for example trusted ingress to
  servers).
  Local devices may initiate the WireGuard handshake on UDP 13231 and then use
  their authenticated 192.168.90.x identity for administration.

VLAN40 — guests

  Allowed to RB5009: DHCP and DNS only under the existing guest rules.
  Other router access is blocked.
  Access to LAN/private networks and guest-to-guest forwarding is blocked.
  Internet access remains allowed.

VLAN60 — servers

  Allowed to RB5009: DNS and ICMP under the existing server rules.
  Other router access is blocked.
  Servers may access the Internet under the existing explicit rule.
  Initiating connections into other private networks is blocked.
  Authenticated WG admins may manage servers using TCP 22/80/443/6443 and ICMP.

VLAN99 — quarantine

  No explicit allow rule exists. Unmatched IPv4 input and forwarding traffic
  reaches the final default-deny rules.


